## Three current findings (all `CONFIRMED` mechanism, `UNVERIFIED` magnitude)

**PERF-A1 — Canvas save path (highest value).** `CanvasStoredReplicas.load` (`CanvasStore.swift:85-97`) does 3-4 unpredicated full-table fetches, and `save()` runs it twice per mutation — once on the live context, once on a fresh context (`CanvasStorePersistence.swift:31,61,93-110`). The mutation helpers (`storedStrokeReplicas`/`storedImageReplicas`/`storedBoardReplicas`, `:492-520`) also fetch whole tables then filter in memory. Per committed stroke: ~9 full-table scans. Separately, `representsSameCommittedValue` reads `replica.payload.count` (`CanvasStore.swift:203`) — `CanvasStrokeItem.payload` is a plain `Data` with no scalar metadata column, so every visible stroke's payload bytes materialize per save. Images already got this fix (`encodedByteCount`/`contentDigest`); strokes didn't. Bounded fix: predicate fetches (the in-memory filters already scope to the selected canvas, so replica semantics are preserved) + a `payloadByteCount` column. `loadReplicas` is injectable, so row-count assertions are testable.

**PERF-A2 — Notes typing path.** Every `noteDraft.body` keystroke publish → `updateNSView` unconditionally replaces `header.rootView` and `accessories.rootView` (`NoteAttachmentTray.swift:1161-1163, 990-1000`) and `layoutDocument` re-reads `fittingSize` on every call and every scroll-view layout pass (`:949-950, 857-862`). The re-rendered header allocates a `RelativeDateTimeFormatter` per eval (`NotesPanelContent.swift:466-468`), and the resolver/ledger still do ~3-4 O(document) string compares per publish (`NoteInlineCards.swift:281-298, 318-342`). Bounded fix: a `bodyRevision` counter for the memo keys, content-token gating on rootView replacement, memoized `fittingSize`.

**PERF-A3 — Notes save path.** `NoteStore.update` calls `NoteInlineAnchor.moved(offset, from:to:)` per inline attachment per autosave (`NoteStore.swift:213-218`) — each call allocates two whole-document UTF-16 arrays (`NoteInlineAnchor.swift:52-64`). One `diffing` hoisted out of the loop makes it k× cheaper with identical offsets.

## Task/panel paths

Largely clean — prior findings verified repaired and excluded: family index O(1) lookups, memoized attachments/snapshots, Equatable rows, `.eventDriven` while visible with no timer, event-driven pointer passthrough, coalesced subtask re-fits, predicated `TaskStore`/`NoteStore` fetches, no reload-on-save, event-driven daily cleanup. Residuals noted (1 Hz hidden-state safety timer, O(n) revision reconciliation) are bounded and deliberate.

No builds, tests, profiling, or app launches were performed; all magnitudes are labeled hypotheses with proposed measurements. No source or test files were touched — the only write is the report file.
